    @Builder allows us to create an object by setting its fields
     step-by-step in a readable way,without needing a large
        constructor or many setter calls.


      @PrePersist and @PreUpdate are JPA lifecycle annotations
         . @PrePersist
      It runs before a new entity is inserted into the database.

      2. @PreUpdate
        It runs before an existing entity is updated in the database.

     RECORD is a special type of class introduced in Java 16. It is mainly used when
     you want to create an object whose purpose is simply to carry data.

     @Pattern is a Bean Validation annotation in Java/Spring Boot. It is mainly used
     when you want to check whether a String follows a particular pattern/format.